`mm/` is a read-only historical reference (`AGENTS.md`, "Current codebase":
*"Historical matrix-viz reference — read-only; do not delete; not product
surface"*). It is unchanged since commit `5ca434d`, and `git log -- mm/` shows
exactly one commit ever touched it (`c7b1f7e feat: add mm`).

* **Licence** — MIT. `mm/LICENSE`: *"Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and
  affiliates."*
* **SHA-256 of `mm/LICENSE`** —
  `cf9b17822d1fcd4ff32ccbe14183386fb3adf6f2ff92dc184130823f7fc28173`
* **Upstream** — `mm/README.md` links <https://bhosmer.github.io/mm> and
  <https://bhosmer.github.io/mm/ref.html>. No upstream repository URL, commit,
  or version is recorded anywhere in this tree: the upstream revision `mm/` was
  taken from is **not verified**.

`apps/web/quatricmorph-workspace` is derived from `mm/`. Its
`LICENSE` reproduces `mm/LICENSE` byte for byte (identical SHA-256, above) and
`apps/web/quatricmorph-workspace/NOTICE.md` records what was carried over,
file by file, and what was deliberately not. `package.json` there declares
`"license": "MIT"`.

**Recorded gap.** No file under `apps/web/quatricmorph-workspace/src/` carries a
per-file copyright header; the MIT notice is present once, in the sibling
`LICENSE`, with the derivation stated in `NOTICE.md` and in `README.md`
§License. Whether that placement is sufficient for a given redistribution is
**not assessed here**.

